<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>">
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <%# Inline styles only: most mail clients drop <style> blocks and every
        class with them. One column, 560px at most, so a phone shows it whole.

        The top of the card is a solid pale-indigo band, with the app's maths
        signs as an <img> beside the lettering (public/mail/math-signs.png,
        transparent, drawn at 240x192 and shown at 100x80) — never behind it.
        Two reasons: with the tile as a background the signs ran through the
        dates, and Gmail's dark mode recolours text and cell colours but not
        background images, so the lettering turned white on a band that
        stayed pale. A plain bgcolor is
        recoloured along with the text, and the signs are a mid-tone indigo
        that reads on the light band and on the dark one. Where images are
        blocked the band is plain and still reads. math-band.png and
        math-band-light.png stay in public/ for the emails already sent.

        The heading is the subject unless a template gives its own — or puts
        its own lines into the band (`content_for :band`), as the weekly report
        does with its dates. %>
  </head>
  <% signs = "#{root_url}mail/math-signs.png" %>
  <body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#f4f4f8;font-family:Nunito,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#1f2133;">
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="background:#f4f4f8;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding:24px 12px;">
          <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="max-width:560px;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e4e4ee;border-radius:20px;border-collapse:separate;overflow:hidden;">
            <tr>
              <td bgcolor="#eef0ff" style="background:#eef0ff;border-radius:19px 19px 0 0;padding:20px 20px 20px 24px;">
                <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                  <tr>
                    <td valign="middle">
                      <div style="font-size:20px;font-weight:900;color:#3730a3;letter-spacing:-.02em;">Wunderkind</div>
                      <%= yield :band %>
                    </td>
                    <td valign="middle" width="100" style="width:100px;padding-left:8px;">
                      <img src="<%= signs %>" width="100" height="80" alt="" style="display:block;border:0;width:100px;height:80px;">
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </table>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:26px 24px 28px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;">
                <% heading = content_for?(:heading) ? yield(:heading) : (message.subject unless content_for?(:band)) %>
                <% if heading.present? %>
                  <h1 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:23px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#1f2133;"><%= heading %></h1>
                <% end %>
                <%= yield %>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
          <% if content_for?(:footer) %>
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="max-width:560px;">
              <tr>
                <td style="padding:16px 8px 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#6b6d85;"><%= yield :footer %></td>
              </tr>
            </table>
          <% end %>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
